 [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder for the maximum number of consecutive loan renewals allowed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate item eligibility within 2 seconds and issue the loan receipt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only the happy path when an item is eligible; omits error handling for ineligible items, invalid or unreadable barcodes, and validation failures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the allowed maximum number of active hold requests\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"References 'the allowed maximum number of active hold requests' without specifying the actual numeric cap anywhere in the specification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-009, which restricts a Member in good standing to at most 5 physical items checked out simultaneously, whereas SD-015 allows up to 8 items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-016\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"21 calendar days from the checkout timestamp\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-010\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-010, which sets the standard loan duration for circulating print books to 14 calendar days, whereas SD-016 sets it to 21 calendar days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-017\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"self-register online with only an email address and immediately check out physical books without Librarian ID verification\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-001, which requires a Librarian to verify government-issued photo ID and record full name, email, and phone number before creating an account.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-011, which holds reserved items on the pickup shelf for exactly 72 hours and automatically cancels uncollected holds to notify the next Member in queue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Chained 'and/or' connectors make it ambiguous which specific combination of actions must occur when an item becomes 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice and omits the actor or service responsible for reviewing, approving, and recording fine waiver requests (and does not specify handling for rejected waivers or amounts above $25.00 USD).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the weak, subjective phrase 'if appropriate' without defining objective criteria for when SMS due-date alerts must be sent or how far before the due date they should be dispatched.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"for TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder for the payment receipt archival retention period.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap on accumulated fines\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-019, which specifies an overdue fine of $0.50 USD per overdue day per item capped at $20.00 USD, whereas SD-025 charges $1.25 USD per day with no cap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"permitted to renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-020, which blocks Members with an unpaid fine balance exceeding $5.00 USD from borrowing or renewing items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron's active loan count ... Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\",\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the undefined term 'Patron' inconsistently instead of the established term 'Member' used throughout the rest of the specification (including SD-001 and SD-009 for the same 5-item borrowing limit).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"return search results quickly even when many users are querying\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'quickly' and 'many users' are vague, unquantified terms lacking explicit latency limits and concurrent user load thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'where possible' is a weak, non-binding phrase that leaves the requirement untestable and fails to specify when highlighting is required versus omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy and acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'sufficient' and 'acceptable response times' are vague qualifiers with no measurable accuracy target or latency threshold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently process large batch MARC21 files without noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'efficiently', 'large', and 'noticeable system slowdown' are vague, unquantified terms without defined batch sizes, throughput targets, or acceptable performance degradation bounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Catalog Service shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States only that active loans or holds must be detected when a Librarian attempts to delete a bibliographic record, without specifying the required action afterward (e.g., blocking deletion and returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder for the database backup execution interval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions in a timely manner and retain them for an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'important', 'in a timely manner', and 'an appropriate period' are vague, undefined terms that omit the specific events to audit, maximum logging delay, and retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Failover Manager shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only logging event FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node is unreachable for more than 10 seconds, omitting the actual failover or recovery action (e.g., promoting a replica, rerouting traffic, or alerting an Administrator).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security and clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'adequate' and 'clear' are vague, subjective terms that do not define required security protocols/standards (e.g., TLS version) or concrete error message criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-002, which requires Member passwords of at least 12 characters containing uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters, whereas SD-038 accepts any password of at least 8 characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"active for 60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-004, which terminates authenticated web portal sessions after 15 minutes of user inactivity, whereas SD-039 keeps sessions active for 60 minutes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt and retrieve forgotten passwords\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-003, which mandates one-way bcrypt hashing (cost factor 12) and forbids storing or exposing plaintext passwords, whereas SD-040 mandates reversible AES-256 encryption for plaintext retrieval.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":218.827591,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12896,"output_tokens":28735,"thinking_tokens":25446,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":41631}}}
